<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\OkfProducer.Core\OkfProducer.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\OkfProducer.CodeGraph.TreeSitter\OkfProducer.CodeGraph.TreeSitter.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\OkfProducer.CodeGraph.Roslyn\OkfProducer.CodeGraph.Roslyn.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting" Version="10.0.10" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.CommandLine" Version="2.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    RID-specific `dotnet tool` packaging (design 7.1). A PORTABLE tool package would carry the
    tree-sitter natives for every RID at once - ~590 MB, and not trimmable by hand, because it is
    `deps.json` that feeds NATIVE_DLL_SEARCH_DIRECTORIES, not the contents of the folder. .NET 10
    can emit one pointer package plus one package per RID (~69 MB each) and `dotnet tool install`
    picks the right one.

    `ToolPackageRuntimeIdentifiers` WITHOUT `RuntimeIdentifiers` fails `dotnet pack` with NETSDK1047.
    That was measured, not reasoned about: both are required, and every sub-package must be pushed,
    not only the pointer.

    Deliberately NOT applied to src/OKF4net.Mcp, which has real users and declares no
    RuntimeIdentifier(s) today - so .NET 10's RID-specific tool behaviour does not touch it.

    No Native AOT here: Roslyn, System.CommandLine and the Generic Host rule it out, and an AOT pack
    would have to be built per OS. Framework-dependent RID-specific is the right form. (The `okf`
    CLI in src/ stays AOT; that is unrelated.)

    NOT covered by any automated test: `producers/` is outside CI by decision (design 8.6), so
    `dotnet pack` and a per-RID `dotnet tool install` are a documented manual release step. See
    producers/README.md.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>okfgen</ToolCommandName>
    <RuntimeIdentifiers>win-x64;linux-x64;osx-arm64</RuntimeIdentifiers>
    <ToolPackageRuntimeIdentifiers>win-x64;linux-x64;osx-arm64</ToolPackageRuntimeIdentifiers>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
